  abstract = {This article outlines the application of a Bayesian method for assessing deviations from normality in the distribution of a variable. We link hypotheses about normality, non-normality and skewness to already defined distribution functions and determine their likelihood on the observed data. The ratio of these likelihoods yields a Bayes factor. The obtained Bayes factors quantify evidence for the hypothesis of normality against the hypothesis of non-normality. Similarly, it quantifies evidence for normality against skewness, but can be extended to include a variety of hypotheses. The proposed methodology is implemented in Shiny, an open-source R package.}
