  abstract = {The sampling method proposed by Metropolis et ai. (1953) requires the simulation of a Markov chain with a specified pi as its stationary distribution. Hastings (1970) outlined a general procedure for constructing and simulating such a Markov chain. The matrix P of transition probabilities is constructed using a defined symmetric function s\textasciicircum{} and an arbitrary transition matrix Q - Here, for a given Q , the relative merits of the two simple choices for s \textbraceleft i suggested by Hastings (1970) are discussed. The optimum choice for 8 ti is shown to be one of these. For the other choice, those 0 are given which are known to make the sampling method based on P asymptotically lees precise than independent sampling.},
